   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote the SMILES below.\n\n**Left to right**\n- **Pyridine:** a 2-amino-3-(trifluoromethoxy)pyridine joined through its C5 to C4 of an imidazole.\n- **Imidazole:** N1 carries the bicyclo[1.1.1]pentane, and C2 carries CH(OH)CH(CH3)2 (the carbinol is drawn with plain bonds, so no stereo).\n- **Bicyclopentane:** one bridgehead is bonded to the imidazole N, and the other bears an NH\u2013C(=O) amide.\n- **Cyclobutane:** a 1,3-disubstituted ring. One carbon carries the amide from the bicyclopentane, and the other carries a C(=O)NH linked to the tert-leucine unit. No stereo is drawn.\n- **tert-Leucine:** the \u03b1-carbon has a hashed bond to N and works out to R.\n- **Hydroxypyrrolidine:** the carboxamide is on a wedge, giving C2 = R, and the OH is on a hash, giving C4 = S.\n- **Amide side chain:** NH\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013aryl with the methyl hashed, giving R. The aryl is a 1,4-phenylene joined to C5 of a 4-methylthiazole.\n\nI assigned each stereocentre from the wedge or hash and the CIP priorities, then converted to @/@@ by permutation. This reading gives (R) at the tert-leucine carbon, (2R,4S) on the pyrrolidine and (R) at the benzylic carbon. That is the reverse of the usual VHL-ligand configuration, but it is what the drawing shows. I did not run a software validity check on the SMILES.\n\nSMILES: Nc1ncc(cc1OC(F)(F)F)-c1cn(c(n1)C(O)C(C)C)C12CC(C1)(C2)NC(=O)C1CC(C1)C(=O)N[C@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@@H](O)C[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@H](C)c1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C"
